### Signup — creates User + Workspace + WorkspaceMember(OWNER), sets session cookie.
POST http://localhost:4000/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@kolumna.dev",
  "password": "password123",
  "name": "Test User"
}

### Same email again — expect 409
POST http://localhost:4000/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@kolumna.dev",
  "password": "password123",
  "name": "Test User"
}

### Bad email — expect 400
POST http://localhost:4000/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "password123",
  "name": "Test User"
}

### Who am I — run this right after signup, VS Code REST Client reuses cookies per file
GET http://localhost:4000/auth/me

### Logout
POST http://localhost:4000/auth/logout

### Me again — expect 401 now
GET http://localhost:4000/auth/me

### Login
POST http://localhost:4000/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@kolumna.dev",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Wrong password — expect 401, generic message
POST http://localhost:4000/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@kolumna.dev",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}
